# upstream/ simulates "some real third-party repo on GitHub" for this example. It's regenerated by setup.sh, not part of what vendoring actually produces, so (unlike vendor/ and vendor.yaml, which ARE committed here, that's the whole point of vendoring) it's not committed.
upstream/

# Standard runtime artifacts, same as every other example.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.backup
.terragraph.auto.tfvars.json
